{t: Bubble House}
{st: Medeski Martin and Wood}
{key: Fm}
{tempo: 92}

{sot: Intro}
| Fm7         | Fm7         | Fm7         | Fm7         |
{eot}

{sot: Theme}
| Fm7         | Fm7         | Fm7         | Fm7         |
| Bb7         | Bb7         | Fm7         | Fm7         |
{eot}

{sot: Break}
| Db7         | C7alt       | Fm7         | Fm7         |
{eot}

{sot: Solo}
| Fm7         | Fm7         | Fm7         | Fm7         |
{eot}

{sov: Notes}
Acid Jazz Groove: Anchored by Chris Wood's hypnotic, repeating bassline in F
Dorian / F minor blues. Keep the tempo steady and deep in the pocket.

Theme Structure: Operates as an extended, blues-influenced funk vamp.
The shift to Bb7 provides a classic IV-chord color before cycling back to the
root Fm7 groove.

Turnaround Stabs: The break uses sharp dominant chromaticism on Db7 and C7alt
to create maximum tension before releasing back into the main bass hook.

Organ / Guitar Voicings: Focus on sparse, percussive stabs on top strings.
Extended voicings like Fm9, Bb13, and C7#9 work best to capture the organ trio
vibe.
{eov}